{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "event_id": "923d5e65-8bcc-4a0f-9773-643ab638435d", "run_id": "R002", "seq": 4, "ts": "2026-11-03T21:45:08.297Z", "type": "note", "actor": "system", "phase": "implement", "condition": "unstructured", "task_id": "T-SPLIT-01", "session_id": "fe2baeca-44dd-4674-bcd6-0c259684a5b9", "payload": {"text": "agent session started", "session_id": "fe2baeca-44dd-4674-bcd6-0c259684a5b9", "source": "hook"}}
{"schema_version": "1.0.0", "event_id": "ec0016da-f87c-4b76-9a5a-e5139709d51f", "run_id": "R002", "seq": 5, "ts": "2026-11-03T21:45:08.447Z", "type": "prompt", "actor": "human", "phase": "implement", "condition": "unstructured", "task_id": "T-SPLIT-01", "session_id": "fe2baeca-44dd-4674-bcd6-0c259684a5b9", "payload": {"text": "Build a command-line tool that reads a CSV file of shared group expenses and prints who owes whom in order to settle up. The CSV has a header row with columns payer, amount, description. The participant list is supplied separately as a comma-separated argument. Every participant owes an equal share of the group total. The tool computes each person's net balance and prints a minimal list of payments that settles every balance to zero. All money is handled in whole cents and rounding must never lose or invent money: the payments printed must sum exactly to the total imbalance. Malformed input (missing file, unknown payer not in the participant list, non-numeric or negative amount, empty participant list) must produce a clear error on stderr and a non-zero exit code. Python 3, standard library only.\n\nRun it as `python -m splitter EXPENSES.csv --participants NAMES`, with the package `splitter` under `src/`. Each payment is printed on its own line as `PAYER pays PAYEE AMOUNT`, with the amount to two decimal places.\n\nExamples, where `trip.csv` contains a header row and the single row `Alice,30.00,Hotel`:\n\n```\n$ python -m splitter trip.csv --participants Alice,Bob\nBob pays Alice 15.00\n\n$ python -m splitter missing.csv --participants Alice,Bob\n(an error message on standard error; a non-zero exit status)\n```", "chars": 1320, "words": 211, "sha256": "2f3d0d58af3ec3ee1a7c1b560122abca6b05443a020b37b49a30933bc03c0787", "source": "hook"}}
